 "notes": [
  "No qal attested for this root; hiphil (the causative \"set apart / make a distinction\" sense, well attested across the plagues narrative in Exodus and in Ps.4.4) is used as the primary/citation stem, with niphal as its natural passive/reflexive counterpart. DEFAULT_STEM_OVERRIDE added (\"פלה\": \"hiphil\") since niphal would otherwise be picked mechanically by STEM_ORDER.",
  "One hiphil form (Ps.17.7, הַפְלֵה חֲסָדֶיךָ, \"show your steadfast love wondrously\") doesn't fit \"set apart; make a distinction\" -- it parallels niphal's \"be wonderful\" sense instead (i.e. hiphil \"make marvelous/show wondrously\"). Kept under hiphil since it's the same stem/root, but flagging the mismatch: 4 of 5 hiphil forms (the Exodus plague-distinction forms, Ps.4.4) support the stored gloss; Ps.17.7 alone supports a third, unlisted shade."
